{
  "_comment": "RETIRED AS A RUNTIME INPUT (task 17, 2026-07-28). ingest/ats.py no longer reads this file on a nightly run: the roster is the `company_ats` table, so adding an employer is an INSERT and not a deploy (16-ats-token-discovery.md:34). This file survives as the ONE-TIME SEED CORPUS behind `python3 ingest/ats.py --seed-from-json`, in the same relationship data/nyc-employer-seed.json has to ats_seed -- idempotent, insert-only, and it never overwrites a row tools/ats-discover.py wrote. Editing it changes nothing until that command is re-run, and re-running it will not resurrect a token deleted from company_ats on purpose. If you want an employer ingested, insert the row. Verified ATS board tokens: each entry was confirmed live via a direct HTTP call to the platform's public job-board API (see method below) on 2026-07-23, which is the date the seed writes as first/last_validated_at rather than stamping today's on a check made in July. job_count_at_verification is a snapshot from 2026-07-23, not live data -- re-fetch at ingest time.",
  "_comment_retired_fields": "is_nyc_hq and is_ai_focused are NO LONGER READ. They were company-level (HQ, not where any individual req is based) and nothing in the repo ever consumed the jobs.company_is_nyc_hq / company_is_ai_focused columns they filled -- verified 2026-07-28: the only references anywhere are the writes in the six ingest scripts and the DDL at schema.py:295-296. company_ats has no column for them and adding one is a schema change out of scope for task 17, so ingest/ats.py now writes NULL, which is what four of the other five sources already write. Kept in this file rather than deleted because it is the only record that the judgement was ever made, and because deleting a hand-assembled signal is not reversible from git alone in six months.",
